# The container entrypoint is executed by /bin/sh inside a linux image. A CRLF checkout
# on a Windows machine breaks it in the least helpful way there is: the shebang line ends
# in \r, so the kernel looks for an interpreter called "/bin/sh\r" and the container exits
# with "no such file or directory" naming a file that is plainly there.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
